Week 3 — Admin Student Management Plan
Contributor: Krishna
Project: Campus Placement and Internship Portal
Module: Admin & Analytics
Week: 3

1. Objective
The objective of Week 3 is to plan and review student management functionality from the administrator's perspective.

The administrator should be able to view student records and manage them according to the application's existing database structure and access-control rules.

2. Scope of Student Management
The planned administrative functionality includes:

Viewing registered student records.
Viewing available student profile information.
Searching for students by appropriate identifying fields.
Reviewing student education and skills information where available.
Viewing relevant student placement and application information.
Managing student records according to authorized administrative permissions.
3. Existing Project Review
Before implementation, the following areas must be inspected:

Existing student database table and columns.
Student-related DAO methods.
Existing servlet routes and controller logic.
JSP pages used for administrative interfaces.
Authentication and authorization rules.
Relationships between students and applications.
The implementation must follow the existing project structure rather than introduce duplicate tables or unnecessary classes.

4. Proposed Administrator Workflow
The authorized administrator opens the student management section.
The application retrieves student records from the existing database.
The administrator views the available student information.
The administrator searches for a particular student when required.
The application displays the matching records.
Any permitted management action is validated and processed.
The administrator receives appropriate success or error feedback.
5. Security Considerations
Only authorized administrators should access administrative student-management operations.
Student information should be displayed only to users with appropriate permissions.
Database queries should use parameterized statements where applicable.
Destructive actions should require suitable confirmation and authorization.
Sensitive student information should not be exposed unnecessarily.
6. Development Tasks
Review the existing student database schema.
Identify reusable DAO methods.
Review the existing administrator navigation.
Plan the student listing interface.
Plan search and filtering functionality.
Identify validation and authorization requirements.
Implement and test selected features in subsequent development work.
7. Expected Deliverables
Student management requirements.
Review of existing database and application components.
Proposed administrator workflow.
List of implementation and testing tasks.
8. Completion Criteria
This planning document is complete when the required functionality, relevant existing components, security considerations, and implementation tasks have been documented.

Actual implementation status must be recorded separately after the corresponding code has been developed and tested.

